/**
@page xt_reference XT reference and API terminology

References in these headers identify the Siemens Parasolid XT Format Reference,
July 2022 edition. Section numbers and printed page numbers refer to that edition,
not to a Parasolid SDK release or a promise of support for every documented type.
The local reading copy is in the workspace directory `xt-doc/pNNN.md`; for example,
page 96 is `xt-doc/p096.md`. The manual is not bundled with this library.

@section xt_terms Terminology and scope

- `FIN` is the schema node name; the conceptual entity is a halfedge. The PK
  interface calls it a fin (section 1.1.1). `FinUse` retains that source identity.
- NodeId stores a decoded stream-local node index (zero is null). It does not
  represent the persistent node-id/identifier described in section 4.3.13.
- Natural curve derivatives follow increasing source parameter; natural surface
  normals follow the cross product of the two parameter derivatives. Curve,
  surface, face and fin senses have different roles (section 5.2.8).
- Wireframe edges bound no faces; ring edges have two null endpoint references.
  An acorn is a shell containing a single isolated vertex.
- Boundary groups, canonical paths, bound geometry, inversion seeds, resource
  budgets and solver profiles are library API concepts, not additional XT nodes.
- Geometric tolerances in the API are explicit caller inputs in source units.
  They do not automatically adopt BODY resolution fields or certify the
  manifold-body restrictions in section 4.5.
- Delta packet inspection and explicit application plans are library contracts.
  The cited manual does not specify the complete internal PMARK/history wire
  protocol; no automatic history semantics are claimed.

